  "A13": [
    {
      "from": "myra",
      "choice": "change",
      "text": "I already have a Stripe account, don't see why we can't just make it live in this setup pass",
      "at": "2026-10-08T15:48:06.804Z"
    },
    {
      "from": "claude",
      "choice": "answer",
      "text": "Yes, that works, and it's free (Stripe only takes its per-payment fee). Two things to keep it clean: **1. Make a separate Stripe account for shwarm** under your same login (Stripe lets one login hold several accounts, free). Then the money, the payout and the statement line (SHWARM) stay apart from your other business. **2. Say plainly who gets the money.** Without a nonprofit, gifts go to you personally, so they're income for you and not tax-deductible for the giver. The donate modal and terms will say \"support shwarm: payments go to Myra Krusemark, who runs it; not tax-deductible.\" (Not tax advice; worth a word with whoever does your taxes.) The modal stays as designed: once or monthly, preset or custom amount, an optional note, through Stripe's hosted checkout. A nonprofit or fiscal host can take over later. Say yes and I'll record A13 as Stripe at launch.",
      "at": "2026-10-08T15:48:23.074298+00:00"
    },
    {
      "from": "myra",
      "choice": "yes",
      "text": "",
      "at": "2026-10-08T15:54:55.225Z"
    },
    {
      "from": "claude",
      "choice": "answer",
      "text": "Recorded in the decision log. A13 is decided.",
      "at": "2026-10-08T15:55:09.828734+00:00"
    }
  ],
  "A14": [
    {
      "from": "myra",
      "choice": "change",
      "text": "whats the problem with it being a repo under myrakrusemark",
      "at": "2026-10-08T15:49:28.954Z"
    },
    {
      "from": "claude",
      "choice": "answer",
      "text": "Honestly, no real problem for the beta. github.com/myrakrusemark/shwarm is less setup, and you're the only maintainer. What an org buys: other maintainers with their own access, a home that can be handed to a nonprofit later, and the platform repo plus the agent-skills repo under one shwarm name instead of your personal one. None of that matters yet, and moving later is cheap: GitHub redirects old repo URLs (web and git) after a transfer. **Revised recommendation:** start under myrakrusemark (repos `shwarm` and `shwarm-skills`), move to an org when a second maintainer joins or an entity forms. Code licenses stay as proposed: server AGPL-3.0, client/CLI/skills MIT. Say yes and I'll record it.",
      "at": "2026-10-08T15:49:40.771842+00:00"
    },
    {
